  		<div id="post-1776" data-postid="1776" data-userid="6173" data-mention="a-r-williams" data-isowner="0" class="post-wrap wpfn-2">
                            <div class="wpforo-post wpfcl-1">
                <div class="wpf-left">
                	                		<div class="author-avatar"><img alt='' src='https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/4b3c560c88be48cb4182280a6633e0e06196e0a767e03e451d5b6066061e6048?s=110&#038;d=mm&#038;r=g' srcset='https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/4b3c560c88be48cb4182280a6633e0e06196e0a767e03e451d5b6066061e6048?s=220&#038;d=mm&#038;r=g 2x' class='avatar avatar-110 photo' height='110' width='110' /></div>
                                        <div class="author-data">
                        <div class="author-name"><span>
                            <i class="fas fa-circle wpfsx wpfcl-0" title="Offline"></i>
            
        </span>&nbsp;<a href="https://writersofthefuture.com/participant/6173/" style=""  title="A.R.Williams">A.R.Williams</a></div>
                        <div class="wpf-author-nicename" title="You can address a user with @nickname in post reply. Note the nickname can be modified in the user profile page.">(@a-r-williams)</div>                                                <div class="wpf-member-profile-buttons">
                                                    </div>
                                                                        <div class="author-posts">
                            Posts: 19                        </div>
                                                                        <div class="author-title">
                            <span class="wpf-member-title wpfrt" title="Rating Title">Active Member</span>                        </div>
                            <div class="author-rating-full"
         style="color:#4dca5c"
         title="Member Rating Badge">
         <i class="fas fa-star"></i>         </div>                                                </div>
                    <div class="wpf-clear"></div>
                </div><!-- left -->
                <div class="wpf-right">
                	<div class="wpforo-post-content-top">
                                                                        <div>&nbsp;</div>
                    	<div class="wpf-post-actions">
							<span class="wpforo-action-buttons-wrap"><span class="wpf-action" data-copy-wpf-furl="https://writersofthefuture.com/forum/interviews-entrants-judges-past-winners/writing-advice-from-gene-wolfe/#post-1776" data-copy-wpf-shurl="https://writersofthefuture.com/forum/postid/1776/" wpf-tooltip-position="left"><i class="fas fa-link wpfsx"></i></span></span>                        </div>
                                            </div>
                    <div class="wpforo-post-content">
                        <p>I often like to construct an ending soon after I write the beginning.</p>
<p>For me, the two are linked. A beginning should be full of possibilities of what the ending could be. And then when you read the ending, you should find the it originates from the beginning.</p>
<br style="margin: 0; padding:0; width:0; height: 0; clear: both">                                                                                                	<div class="wpforo-post-signature"><p><arel="nofollow nofollow" target="_blank" href="http://a-r-williams.com">http&#058;//a-r-williams&#046;com</a></p>
<p>HM x 1</p>
</div>                                                <div class="wpf-post-button-actions">
                                                        <div>&nbsp;</div>
                            <span class="wpforo-action-buttons-wrap"><span class="wpf-action not_reg_user"><i class="fas fa-reply fa-rotate-180"></i></span><span wpf-tooltip="Quote" class="wpf-action not_reg_user"><i class="fas fa-quote-left wpfsx"></i></span></span>                        </div>
	                                                                </div>
                    <div class="wpforo-post-content-bottom">
                    	<div class="cbleft wpfcl-0">
                            Posted : November 28, 2010 3:31 am		                    <div class="reacted-users"></div>						</div>
                    	<div class="wpf-clear"></div>
                    </div>
                </div><!-- right -->
